course: dictionary
lesson: 5474
title: Lasagne: a dish and its layers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the words around them show you which meaning is right. «Garfield wolfs a tray of lasagne» tells you lasagne is food, because you eat it from a tray.
explain: The dictionary says lasagne is an Italian dish of flat sheets of pasta, built up in layers with meat or vegetable sauce and cheese, then baked in an oven. Read the clues in «Pets need proper food made for their kind; rich human food, like a cat eating lasagne, can make them ill» and you can see it is a rich human food.
explain: Lasagne can also mean the wide, flat sheets of pasta themselves. When you read a word, ask: what does this sentence need? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Lasagne is an Italian dish.
fact: Lasagne is made of flat sheets of pasta, in layers, with meat or vegetable sauce and cheese.
fact: Lasagne is baked in an oven.
fact: Lasagne can also mean the flat sheets of pasta themselves.
fact: «Vegetable lasagne» has a vegetable sauce instead of a meat sauce.
exercise: What is lasagne? | A kind of bread roll | *An Italian dish of pasta layers, sauce and cheese, baked in an oven | A type of fish | A sweet pudding made of rice
exercise: «Pets need proper food made for their kind; rich human food, like a cat eating lasagne, can make them ill.» Why can lasagne make a cat ill? | Because lasagne is always made of fish | *Because it is rich human food, not food made for cats | Because it is too cold to eat | Because cats only eat in the morning
exercise: Lasagne can mean the pasta sheets. Which is the second meaning? | *The wide, flat sheets of pasta | A baking tin | A kind of sauce | A cheese grater
test: What does «layers of lasagne» show about the dish? | *It is built up in several flat layers | It is served cold in a glass | It has only one thin sheet | It is a drink
test: What is vegetable lasagne? | *Lasagne with a vegetable sauce instead of meat | Lasagne made only of fish | Lasagne with no pasta at all | Lasagne eaten with a spoon of ice cream
exam: Which is the plural of one dish of lasagne? | *lasagnes | lasagnaes | lasagnis | lasagnies
